          "filename": "Hello Milky Way (220754185).jpeg",
          "caption": "500px provided description: We were on our way back from arch rock - Joshua Tree - California and I decided to stop by a quite spot to get a tracked shot of the MW because I couldn't set up my tracker in Arch Rock because of the crowd. A shooting star decided to come and say hi in my trial composition shot, so I cut the meteor and stacked it to my final composition. The shot was tracked for the sky and stacked with a still foreground shot.\nI did lens profile correction and enhancement in LR and PS. I added a slight glare to the head of the shooting star because I feel that looks cool.\nThe sky/background settings: 2.5 minutes exposure tracked with a skyguider pro. / ISO 800 / 16 mm / f/2.8 1 exposure\nForeground:\n\n45 sec / f/2.8 / ISO 1600 1 exposure. [#sky ,#landscape ,#light ,#moon ,#silhouette ,#evening ,#mountain ,#weather ,#space ,#storm ,#exploration ,#telescope ,#dusk ,#astronomy ,#joshua tree ,#milky way ,#astrophotography ,#observatory ,#meteor ,#galaxy ,#night photography ,#nightscape ,#constellation ,#shooting star ,#calamity ,#meteor shower ,#no person ,#Orion]",
